        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Postmodernism and After",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "EXAMPLES FROM HISTORY:\n  Venturi demonstrates that the great buildings of history are\n  COMPLEX and CONTRADICTORY — not simple and unified.\n  The Parthenon's subtle refinements (entasis, stylobate curve):\n    simultaneously regular AND irregular.\n  Borromini's facades: simultaneously convex AND concave.\n  Michelangelo's Laurentian Library vestibule: columns that\n    don't support anything (bracketed out from the wall),\n    staircases that won't let you walk normally."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-POSTMODERNISM.md#014",
      "path": [
        "07-POSTMODERNISM.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:architecture-history:07-postmodernism, git-history:architecture-history:07-postmodernism]",
