        "root_concepts": "[postmodernism]",
        "section": "architecture-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Postmodernism and After",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "MODERNISM'S PROBLEM (per Venturi):\n  Modernism's exclusions (no ornament, no history, pure function)\n  are impoverishments.\n  \"Less is a bore.\"\n  Complexity is not failure — it is richness.\n  Buildings communicate. They communicate culturally, symbolically,\n  through reference and memory.\n  Modernism's willful amnesia about history cuts buildings off\n  from the communication system buildings have always used."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-POSTMODERNISM.md#015",
      "path": [
        "07-POSTMODERNISM.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
