        "root_concepts": "[postmodernism]",
        "section": "architecture-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Postmodernism and After",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "VERSUS FUNCTIONALISM:\n  \"A building can be more than a diagram of its function\"\n  Function is necessary but not sufficient for architecture.\n  The hospital is functional. The church is functional. But they\n  must also mean something — and meaning requires reference.\n```"
    },
