      },
      "text": "MAIN STREET IS ALMOST ALL RIGHT:\n  Commercial vernacular (strip malls, signs, parking lots)\n  was despised by modernist planners (=visual pollution).\n  Venturi: this IS the built environment of American democracy.\n  Don't plan it away. Understand it. Learn from it.\n  This was provocative in 1972. It still is.\n```"
